  "conclusion": [
    "Across 43320 TX-RX link-samples, the geometric (position-exact) model finds 81.1% to be NLOSv. The density-based probabilistic model, choosing its most-likely class, recovers only 8.0% of those (miss rate 92.0%) and raises false NLOSv alarms on 4.6% of the genuinely clear links.",
    "It misclassifies 80.3% of links outright (hard) and a draw disagrees with the geometric truth 73.1% of the time (soft). Its P(NLOSv) is poorly calibrated against the actual geometry: Brier score 0.543, ECE 0.593.",
    "This costs 7.3 dB mean absolute pathloss error (bias +2.5 dB, p95 17.3 dB) versus the position-exact model.",
    "Because NLOSv blockage is governed by where the platoon vehicles actually are -- not by a global density tier -- no single density setting reproduces the per-link geometric verdict. For V2X groupcast adaptation, which depends on accurate per-link CSI, position-exact geometric NLOSv determination is the correct choice."
  ],
